    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">After updating geomorph (and R) warpRefMesh is giving an error:<div><br></div><div><div>Error in xyz.coords(digitspec[1:fixed, ]) : </div><div>  &#39;x&#39;, &#39;y&#39; and &#39;z&#39; lengths differ</div></div><div><br></div><div>My code worked fine before the update, and I have doublechecked the reference and target coordinates, and both have the same structure and definitely the same dimensions: num [1:53, 1:3] <div><br></div><div>As an example (from a previous group post):</div><div><br></div><div><div>data(&quot;scallopPLY&quot;)</div><div>data(&quot;scallops&quot;)</div><div>warpRefMesh(scallopPLY$ply, scallops$coorddata[,,1], mshape(scallops$coorddata))</div></div><div><br></div><div>This gives me the same error.</div></div><div><br></div><div>Any thoughts appreciated.</div><div>___________________________</div><div><div>Dr. Faysal Bibi</div><div>Senior Scientist</div><div>Museum für Naturkunde</div><div>Invalidenstr. 43</div><div>10115 Berlin, Germany</div></div></div>"
